From ece75e856fc6477fe9a75c87ee2c61b61a216e2e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HandSonic <8078023+handsonic@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 22:29:12 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] net: airoha: unwind failed phylink opens

If airoha_set_vip_for_gdm_port() fails during device open, phylink has
already been connected and started. Stop queues and disconnect phylink on
that error path so the next open starts from a clean state.

Signed-off-by: HandSonic <8078023+handsonic@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
index 7a08a4280..fbf7a8705 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
@@ -2559,8 +2559,12 @@ static int airoha_dev_open(struct net_device *netdev)
 
 	netif_tx_start_all_queues(netdev);
 	err = airoha_set_vip_for_gdm_port(dev, true);
-	if (err)
+	if (err) {
+		netif_tx_disable(netdev);
+		phylink_stop(dev->phylink);
+		phylink_disconnect_phy(dev->phylink);
 		return err;
+	}
 
 	/* It seems GDM3 and GDM4 needs SPORT enabled to correctly work */
 	if (netdev_uses_dsa(netdev) || port->id > 2)
